        "content": "<p>Gelbpunkt opened <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14771\">PR #14771</a> from <code>Gelbpunkt:s390x-128bit-atomic-cas</code> to <code>bytecodealliance:main</code>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Depends on #14770 </p>\n<hr>\n<p>This adds and makes use of the <code>CDSG</code> instruction. Since the 128-bit integers are stored in VRs and <code>CDSG</code> operates on <code>RegPair</code>s, we need to introduce some helpers to move data between VRs and <code>RegPair</code>s by extracting or inserting two lanes of <code>I64</code>s.</p>\n<p>I've verified this in qemu-user and on a z15 inside z/VM with the atomic-128 runtest, but we're missing an implementation of <code>atomic_rmw</code> before that can be enabled on s390x.</p>\n<hr>\n<p>I'm not sure where to put these helpers, if there's a better place than <code>lower.isle</code>, which I suspect there may be, please let me know :)</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 631936585,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1792067096
    },
